<header>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="sub">Fruit Sort Neon Edition (com.mindcraftstudio.fruitsort) &middot; by MINDCRAFT STUDIO<br>Last updated: 31 October 2026</p>
</header>

<p>This Privacy Policy explains what information is processed when you play <strong>Fruit Sort Neon Edition</strong> (the &ldquo;Game&rdquo;), an Android puzzle game published by MINDCRAFT STUDIO (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;). By using the Game you agree to the practices described here.</p>

<h2>1. Summary</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The Game has no user accounts, and we do not ask you for your name, email address, phone number, or any other personal details.</li>
  <li>Your game progress and settings are stored only on your device.</li>
  <li>The Game shows ads provided by <strong>Google AdMob</strong>. AdMob may collect and use certain device and usage data to serve and measure ads, as explained in section 3.</li>
  <li>Where required by law (for example in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland), we ask for your consent before ads are requested.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Information stored on your device</h2>
<p>The Game saves your level progress, stars, scores, language choice, sound settings and similar preferences in the local storage of the app on your device. This data stays on your device. We do not receive it and we cannot access it. It is removed when you uninstall the Game or clear its data in your Android settings.</p>

<h2>3. Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
<p>The Game displays banner, interstitial and rewarded video ads using Google AdMob. Rewarded ads are optional: you choose to watch one in exchange for a bonus such as extra time. When ads are requested or shown, Google and its partners may collect and process the following information from your device:</p>
<div class="tablewrap">
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Typical purposes</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Advertising ID and other device identifiers</td><td>Showing and measuring ads, analytics, fraud prevention and security</td></tr>
    <tr><td>IP address and approximate location (derived from the IP address)</td><td>Showing relevant ads, analytics, fraud prevention</td></tr>
    <tr><td>App interactions (for example ad impressions, taps and views)</td><td>Ad delivery and measurement, analytics</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Diagnostics (crash logs and performance data)</td><td>Keeping the ad service stable and secure, analytics</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>We do not receive this data and we do not combine it with any other information about you. Google acts as an independent controller of the data it collects through AdMob. To learn how Google uses information from apps that use its services, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a> and the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

<h2>4. Your choices and consent</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Consent (EEA, UK, Switzerland).</strong> In regions where the law requires it, the Game shows a consent message provided by Google&rsquo;s User Messaging Platform when you first open it. You can accept, manage your options, or decline. If privacy options are available for your region, a privacy button in the Game&rsquo;s menu lets you review or change your choice at any time.</li>
  <li><strong>Advertising ID.</strong> You can reset your advertising ID or opt out of personalised ads in your Android settings (for example Settings &rarr; Google &rarr; Ads; the exact path can differ by device and Android version).</li>
  <li><strong>Rewarded ads</strong> are always optional and the Game can be played without watching them.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Children</h2>
<p>The Game is intended for a general audience aged 13 and over and is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided information through the Game, please contact us and we will help to resolve it.</p>

<h2>6. Data sharing and retention</h2>
<p>We do not sell personal information. The only third party that receives data through the Game is Google (AdMob), as described above. Data collected by Google is retained according to Google&rsquo;s own policies. Data stored by the Game on your device is kept until you delete it or uninstall the Game.</p>

<h2>7. Security</h2>
<p>Network communication with the ad service is encrypted in transit. Because the Game stores its data on your device only, the security of that data also depends on the security of your device.</p>

<h2>8. Your rights</h2>
<p>Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR in the EEA and UK), you may have rights to access, correct, delete or restrict the use of your personal data, to object to its processing, and to withdraw consent at any time. Because we do not hold personal data about you, requests relating to advertising data are handled by Google; you can use the controls in section 4 or Google&rsquo;s privacy tools at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/" rel="noopener">myaccount.google.com</a>. You may also contact us with any question and we will respond as soon as we can.</p>

<h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>We may update this policy from time to time, for example when the Game&rsquo;s features change. The &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date above shows the latest version. Continued use of the Game after an update means you accept the revised policy.</p>

